---
source: crates/tk/tests/scenarios.rs
expression: "p.run(\"--help\")"
---
Repository-local work tracker

Usage: tk <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add          Create a local Ticket or Epic
  accept       Accept a triage Ticket into ranked, selectable work
  park         Hold an accepted Ticket out of automatic selection, keeping its Priority
  unpark       Return a parked Ticket to accepted, selectable work
  init         Initialize the Repository Store in the current Git repository
  list         Render the Repository Store List Tree
  next         Select the next ready Ticket
  show         Render one Ticket or Epic with current state
  search       Find Tickets and Epics by a title substring
  grep         Search title and body text for a regular expression, with match context
  update       Update the title, body, priority, or parent of a Ticket or Epic
  start        Mark a Ticket or Epic active
  stop         Return a Ticket or Epic to open
  done         Close a Ticket or Epic
  block        Record that one item blocks another
  unblock      Remove a blocking relationship
  prime        Print the agent workflow briefing
  manpage      Print or install the tk manpage
  self-update  Replace the running tk binary with the latest release
  remote       Configure the Primary Backend
  sync         Apply pending Mutations through the configured Remote
  promote      Promote a Local Ticket or Epic through the configured Remote
  adopt        Adopt an existing Backend issue into the local working set
  detach       Keep a Backend Item as local work without changing the Backend object

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
